cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use spotgp in your research, please cite the software release and the
  companion papers listed under "preferred-citation" and "references".
title: "spotgp: Gaussian Process kernels for stellar variability from starspot models"
type: software
version: 1.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jbirky/spotgp"
url: "https://spotgp.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  spotgp provides a Gaussian process kernel for stellar photometric variability
  that is derived analytically from a model of starspots on a differentially
  rotating star, so that every kernel hyperparameter (equatorial rotation
  period, differential rotation shear, inclination, spot lifetime and
  emergence/decay timescale, and amplitude) is a physical quantity. It is
  implemented in JAX with a banded Cholesky solver, a matched forward
  light-curve simulator, and interfaces to gradient-based and nested samplers.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - Gaussian processes
  - stellar rotation
  - starspots
  - differential rotation
  - JAX
authors:
